<details id="image-editor-panel" class="image-editor-panel"><summary>Add or edit an article image</summary>
<p class="small">Use an existing public HTTPS image URL. Select a Word image placeholder or ordinary article text to replace it, or place a new image at the article end. Paragraph breaks keep the image separate. No image is loaded, uploaded, or checked here.</p>
<div class="actions"><button id="image-use-selection" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Use current article selection</button><button id="image-at-end" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Place at article end</button></div>
<div id="image-placeholder-choices" hidden><label for="image-placeholder-select">Omitted Word image to replace</label><select id="image-placeholder-select"></select><button id="image-use-placeholder" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Use selected Word placeholder</button><p id="image-placeholder-limit" class="small"></p></div>
<p id="image-target-status" class="small">Choose a location before preparing a change.</p>
<label for="image-url">Image URL (HTTPS)</label><textarea id="image-url" rows="2" inputmode="url" maxlength="2048" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" disabled aria-describedby="image-url-help"></textarea><p id="image-url-help" class="small">A direct image file URL, up to 2,048 characters. No credentials, spaces, or quoted titles. The address is preserved as entered.</p>
<label for="image-alt">Alternative text</label><textarea id="image-alt" rows="2" maxlength="500" disabled aria-describedby="image-alt-help"></textarea><p id="image-alt-help" class="small">Describe the image's purpose in this article, up to 500 characters on one line. For an intentionally decorative image, clear this field and select the option below.</p>
<label class="check"><input id="image-decorative" type="checkbox" disabled><span>This image is decorative and should have empty alternative text</span></label>
<button id="image-preview" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Preview image change</button>
<div id="image-change-preview" hidden><h3>Review the exact replacement</h3><p class="small">Only the selected text is replaced. Added paragraph breaks appear below. The rest of the article is kept exactly.</p><label for="image-before">Selected text to remove</label><textarea id="image-before" rows="3" readonly></textarea><label for="image-after">Markdown to insert, including paragraph breaks</label><textarea id="image-after" rows="4" readonly></textarea></div>
<div class="actions"><button id="image-apply" type="button" class="button" disabled>Apply image change</button><button id="image-discard" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Discard image preparation</button></div>
<p id="image-editor-status" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Image editor is loading. You can edit Markdown directly.</p>
<p class="small">Applying saves a checkpoint and clears export approval and the linked-image choice. For WordPress, open Images for WordPress and explicitly choose linked Image blocks afterward. Other exports keep image Markdown as text. Unsaved image preparation is excluded from backups, collections, and exports; apply it first to keep it. <a href="/help/publishing-handoff/#image-editor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image editing help (new tab)</a></p>
</details>
